One more consideration: in `_reorient`, when the label matches, I copy the children. But the children of those children are shared references (shallow copy of the list, but I'm creating new Tree nodes for each child with `list(c.children)` — a shallow copy of the list; the grandchildren are shared). As long as I don't mutate the shared grandchildren, it's fine. In the deeper case, I create new Tree nodes for the siblings along the path. Since I never mutate the input tree, sharing is fine.

